Two mechanical compatibility fixes to wasm3 v0.5.0's meta-WASI layer (source/m3_api_meta_wasi.c, 2021) against the current wasi-libc, applied to the pinned source before the zig build.
wasi-libc has since renamed the __wasi_filestat_t fields (st_dev to dev, and so on) and switched the __wasi_path_* functions from (pointer, length) pairs to null-terminated strings.
The fix renames the fields and copies each guest-supplied path through a bounded null-terminating buffer (m3_nt_path); behavior is otherwise unchanged.
The layer forwards the guest's WASI calls to the outer host, which is what lets the converted interpreter serve its guest through dewasm's own WASI runtime.
Tied to the v0.5.0 line shape: a pin bump regenerates this patch against the new source, not a rebase.

